# What goes into the source distribution.
#
# This file exists because the sdist is NOT safe by default here. setuptools auto-includes a
# top-level `tests/` directory, and this repository is checked out inside the polyp benchmark
# audit's own working tree, so a plain `python -m build` from the project root swept the audit's
# entire 41-file suite into the tarball, `test_paper_draft.py` included: 63 KB of assertions about
# an unpublished manuscript, in a package about to be uploaded to PyPI. The tarball went from
# 19 KB to 128 KB and would have published the audit.
#
# Building from a clean `git archive` avoided it, but that is a procedure someone has to remember.
# Pruning here makes the build correct from any directory, and
# `groupeval/tests/test_packaging.py` asserts the result.

include LICENSE
include README.md
include CITATION.cff
include pyproject.toml
recursive-include groupeval *.py *.md

prune tests
prune src
prune results
prune data
prune logs
prune figures
prune node_modules
global-exclude *.py[cod]
global-exclude __pycache__
